{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\left(\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i}\\right)|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j}\n=\n\\left(\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_j}\\right)|_{\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j \\to \\mathcal{C}/U_i \\to \\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}/U_i \\times_U U_j \\to \\mathcal{C}/U_j \\to \\mathcal{C}/U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b1d3f208f75d5ae26e96a352f62e4166188d7288a7dbaf461183327b8ca486e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1957a488c4a4154d5758bac338af5ac0288341ac4b17236fa293d8f733d7a252", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a covering of <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf on <MATH_0005>.\nAssociated to <MATH_0006> we have its\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>canonical glueing data<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> given by the restrictions\n<MATH_0007> and the canonical isomorphisms\n<MATH_0008>\ncoming from the fact that the composition of the functors\n<MATH_0009>\nand\n<MATH_0010>\nare equal.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c49d6aed214a841188c33c70fed27492b0c934d57a970eaa070c2c2ce5c4706c", "unit_id": "tag:04TP:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/U)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-mapping-property-glue}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9f61547cf972c8942a3aaa4b1cd68ec0a92e8848b858bd19e1c896404c963738", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8e80246892801669d5cb731e9c45c49e228fc69921f6c679d2aaab0ccc8000fc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a covering of <MATH_0003>.\nThe category <MATH_0004> is equivalent\nto the category of glueing data via the functor that associates\nto <MATH_0005> on <MATH_0006> the canonical glueing data.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:702fa325f49f5a68acf14c5dc78e607b99a49c49df914d028a1125de7bb4b125", "unit_id": "tag:04TS:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-glue-maps}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-glue-sheaves}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:34ec2068b95a1ec8756be4a7ab3368c5787a23461227076a9a5cd1729df5e840", "source_text": "In\nLemma <REF_0001>\nwe saw that the functor is fully faithful, and in\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe proved that it is essentially surjective (by explicitly constructing\na quasi-inverse functor).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8379c09a991a5d4fd50e90efe1ef44868d7ae39890e9f9974dc150ace6d3c49f", "unit_id": "tag:04TS:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}_U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0007": "$j_f : \\mathcal{C}/V \\rightarrow \\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0008": "$f : V \\rightarrow U$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$(a : W \\to V) \\mapsto (f \\circ a : W \\to U)$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$$\nc_f : j_f^{-1} \\mathcal{F}_U \\to \\mathcal{F}_V\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0014": "$g : W \\to V$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0016": "$c_g \\circ j_{g}^{-1} c_f$", "MATH_0017": "$c_{f \\circ g}$", "MATH_0018": "$(\\mathcal{F}_{U}, c_f)$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0020": "$(\\mathcal{F}_{U}, c_f) \\to (\\mathcal{G}_{U}, c'_f)$", "MATH_0021": "$(\\varphi_U)$", "MATH_0022": "$\\varphi_U : \\mathcal{F}_U \\to \\mathcal{G}_U$", "MATH_0023": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nj_f^{-1} \\mathcal{F}_U \\ar[r]_{c_f} \\ar[d]_{j_f^{-1} \\varphi_U} &\n\\mathcal{F}_V \\ar[d]^{\\varphi_V} \\\\\nj_f^{-1} \\mathcal{G}_U \\ar[r]^{c'_f} &\n\\mathcal{G}_V\n}\n$$", "MATH_0024": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0025": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0028": "$(\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U},c_f)$", "MATH_0029": "$c_f : j_f^{-1} \\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U} \\to\n\\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/V}$", "MATH_0030": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0031": "$j_V = j_U \\circ j_f$", "MATH_0032": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0033": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0034": "$(\\varphi|_{\\mathcal{C}/U})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-relocalize}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:35077ed1365c4c1523e258e909a780d4d06c55e4fd6ef61de88ed0d7a2b42957", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62dae9cc0f0e65e462339e948b4a5f131a1bd51ebbc28660e7d651557e965924", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a site. We are going to discuss\na version of glueing sheaves on the entire site <MATH_0002>.\nFor each object <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004>, let <MATH_0005>\nbe a sheaf on <MATH_0006>. Recall that there is a functor\n<MATH_0007> associated to each\nmorphism <MATH_0008> in <MATH_0009>, given by\n<MATH_0010>. For each such <MATH_0011>, let\n<MATH_0012>\nbe an isomorphism of sheaves. Assume that given any two arrows\n<MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014> in <MATH_0015>, the composition\n<MATH_0016> is equal to <MATH_0017>. We will call\nsuch a collection of data <MATH_0018> an\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>absolute glueing data for sheaves of sets on <MATH_0019><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\nA morphism of absolute glueing data\n<MATH_0020>\nis given by a collection <MATH_0021>\nof morphisms of sheaves <MATH_0022>,\nsuch that\n<MATH_0023>\ncommutes for every morphism <MATH_0024> in <MATH_0025>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nAssociated to any sheaf <MATH_0026> on <MATH_0027> is its\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>canonical absolute glueing data<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> <MATH_0028>,\nwhere the canonical isomorphisms\n<MATH_0029>\nfor <MATH_0030> come from the relation\n<MATH_0031> as in Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAny morphism <MATH_0032>\nof sheaves of <MATH_0033> induces a morphism\n<MATH_0034> of canonical absolute glueing data.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:573c2c885230a22b28c025289d8d0ef7bc7110889e9fadf5f2fe77626f0a30e0", "unit_id": "tag:04TP:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-glue-sheaves-absolute}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:12d93fde37bcd92638ceb1c291e2eb51af6306d7ce50d57b74dddbcb2f6346e0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2e8b75ebb0acfcdbd531647bcdc9b12ca34ee9639abb59ce16b2de1cff0b75bc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. The category\n<MATH_0002> is equivalent to the category\nof absolute glueing data via the functor that\nassociates to <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004> the\ncanonical absolute glueing data.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a088b556bbf09968dd3ba7c3ce16368d8832ee23f8853888763abadb4eec519", "unit_id": "tag:0GWK:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04TP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{F}_U, c_f)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) = \\mathcal{F}_U(U)$", "MATH_0005": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F}_U(U) \\ar[r] \\ar@{=}[d] &\n\\mathcal{F}_U(V) \\ar[r]^{c_f} &\n\\mathcal{F}_V(V) \\ar@{=}[d] \\\\\n\\mathcal{F}(U) \\ar[rr] &  &\n\\mathcal{F}(V)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$c_g \\circ j_{g}^{-1} c_f = c_{f \\circ g}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0009": "$c_f : \\mathcal{F}_U(V) \\to \\mathcal{F}(V)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}_U \\to \\mathcal{F}|_{\\mathcal{C}/U}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}_U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\mathcal{F}_U, c_f) \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a98ef975b0803c5efead7023bf2d1ca3c232ca23efe24290f2565dd58ef08a90", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f1a2319e1ef212c1513a74f45d16c9668b36453199aa55044c32751d712b7835", "source_text": "Given an absolute glueing data <MATH_0001>,\nwe construct a sheaf <MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003> by\nsetting <MATH_0004>, where restriction\nalong <MATH_0005> given by the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nThe compatibility condition <MATH_0007>\nensures that <MATH_0008> is a presheaf, and also ensures that the maps\n<MATH_0009> define an isomorphism\n<MATH_0010> for each <MATH_0011>.\nSince each <MATH_0012> is a sheaf, this implies that <MATH_0013>\nis a sheaf as well. The functor <MATH_0014>\njust constructed is quasi-inverse to the functor which takes a sheaf\non <MATH_0015> to its canonical glueing data. Further details omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9f04b690062af89be2703f4dae6581a7c638523e2c6f59d09b5954073ab943c", "unit_id": "tag:0GWK:proof"}
